    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into the exploitable matchup against Gusto. The strongest play on the board is **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.82), who benefits from a high-efficiency 19% SP skill boost and an advantageous #2 spot in the order. He is closely followed by **Luis Arraez** (64.64) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.50), both of whom capitalize on the favorable SP skill profile and the added benefit of the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which creates a prime environment for our stolen base pursuit. While **Tyler Freeman** (62.19) carries a lower base, his park factor (+14%) provides the necessary ceiling to elevate him into our elite start category, offsetting the minor risk posed by the opponent's catcher arm.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the bottom of the order involved **Jeremiah Jackson**, who finished just outside the starting rotation at 38.07. While **Jeremiah Jackson** shows potential, the uncertainty of his #9 lineup spot paired with the heavy penalty from the tougher matchup against Sheehan relegated him to the bench. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Bryson Stott** (47.71) and **Taylor Ward** (44.15). While **Bryson Stott** is battling a significant platoon disadvantage against Peterson, his role as an elite hold for stolen bases keeps him in the lineup. **Taylor Ward** faces similar volatility due to an elite opposing arm in Sheehan; he remains in the starting 10 only by virtue of his projected leadoff position. We remain sidelined on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Lawrence Butler** due to ongoing injury or rest, and we will continue monitoring the wire for any late movement involving depth pieces like **Daulton Varsho**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Brendan Donovan** to ensure our daily caps are optimized.",
